WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.400
Film Courage: When you’re writing a&nbsp;
screenplay do you ever think about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:04.400
the money you will make off&nbsp;
of it as you’re writing it?

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:09.520
Mark Sanderson, Screenwriter/Author: No,&nbsp;
because I already have a contract so I know.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:18.240
Now a spec, yes you can have delusions&nbsp;
of grandeur as much as you want but after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:21.680
years in the business you know the&nbsp;
realities of like okay but no you shouldn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:26.960
write from a place of that you should forget&nbsp;
about all that like I said you should do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:32.960
your best job ever if you’re paid $500&nbsp;
buck or 5 million bucks there should be no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:39.240
difference in your desire because then what&nbsp;
you’re doing is you are chasing money. There&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:45.520
are other businesses to do that that are&nbsp;
far more lucrative than spending years of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:49.120
your life toiling away and trying to have that&nbsp;
one… “This is the one that is going to do it!”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:58.240
So no, you should just bathe in the creative&nbsp;
process and not…when you are writing your specs.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:02.320
When you’re writing an assignment and you already&nbsp;
have a contract you know what you are making&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:08.080
and then it becomes stressful because you are&nbsp;
actually making something so you are like “Oh&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:14.080
shoot - this is due when? Ahh…this better be&nbsp;
good.” You know? This is what they are paying me&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:20.240
for so that comes at a different level when you&nbsp;
leap over into that different realm of working&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:27.120
like we discussed earlier about being creative&nbsp;
under a deadline than just toiling away you can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:31.840
work, it’s great to work when you&nbsp;
want…you know my spec…I’m just doing…I’m&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:40.080
not working with anybody else this is all my&nbsp;
words…which it has to be to get to a certain point&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:45.440
absolutely but then you step over that line&nbsp;
into the other world and it’s like “Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:51.360
we don’t like the ending.” And then it&nbsp;
becomes like they say in filmmaking a million&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:58.080
compromises to get something done and sadly&nbsp;
yeah, but to get something done is amazing.

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:02.800
Film Courage: And does that go back to&nbsp;
what we were talking about with the Tai Chi&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:09.040
or the Karate example which is part of it’s the&nbsp;
physical and part of it is the mental and maybe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:13.120
that pressure and maybe this pressure of “I’ve&nbsp;
got to be creative and I’ve got a deadline” and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:16.960
not cracking under that pressure?

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:22.960
Mark: Sure, it’s a lot of it. I mean tremendous&nbsp;
amount of this is mental at the end of the day but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:30.640
then those disciplines you can fall back on&nbsp;
because you can get into this terrible wheel that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:36.480
you’re not producing at the best level you can&nbsp;
because you’re too worried about the other thing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:45.760
If you just yourself and dive into the work you’ll&nbsp;
get it done if you’re not constantly worried about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:50.775
“Well I’ve got eight days left.” Just do it.
Question for the viewers:

00:02:50.775 --> 00:02:53.653
Do you think about how much money you&nbsp;
are going to make with your screenplay?

